# RPost workflow

- Mainline only: topics + outlines → human pick → write/polish → finalize QMD → Actions render/Pages.
- `topics/index.json` is the topic source; `topics/index.md` is generated. Posts live under `content/posts/`.
- Read shared prompts through `prompt-rules/index.json`.
- Choose exactly one category slug: `r-plot`, `r-stats`, `r-base`, `r-tidyverse`, or `r-code-management`.
- Preserve explicit user headings, order, examples, and output requirements.
- When a candidate becomes an article, update its `article` metadata and regenerate `topics/index.md`.
- Never create a permanent images folder; rendered Markdown embeds images.
- Do not add scheduling, rank, or automatic daily writing fields to topics or article manifests. WeChat lineup lives only in `wechat/queue.json`.
- Front stages need human approval; post-QMD render is automated. Follow `AGENTS.md`.
